{"clock":1,"nonce":"7bae91b9072fc2dd6ad7d8997eedfbbe","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792670535,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5978897776"},"data":{"body":"The issue page has an Issue / Cycle switch, so one issue lives on two pages. The cycle reads criteria only under a heading named \"Acceptance criteria\": GB-31's four, under \"Expected\", weren't seen, and writing one from the Cycle view appended a second list.\n\nDecided with the user on 2026-10-21, on the canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/8Eg2APMyeSMGLk5hB1SqCq (rows 4 and 5):\n- **One page.** The current step is the main screen. A done step reopens. A later step is locked, and says why, until its evidence exists. Step 1, Intent, is the issue's description and discussion.\n- **A protocol in `[cycle]`** says where each step's evidence lives and which rule applies, by kind and risk, with defaults for everything.\n- **The statuses are the stages.** Each step's button moves the status.\n- **Step 3 starts the branch** with wtx, and a draft PR holds the plan. Review opens when that PR is marked ready.\n- **Step 4 runs the declared test suites.** Lint, format and type-check run locally, and gate Ready for review.\n- **Each step has its own discussion,** and the agent takes part in it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `docs/prd/cycle-protocol.md` is written and approved by the user before any code.\n- The protocol: criteria headings as a list (Acceptance criteria, Done when, Expected), rules by kind and risk, and defaults that keep today's behaviour.\n- Each step's button moves the status. Without a validation status, Verify happens after the merge and its sign-off closes the issue.\n- One page: a step bar with done, current and locked steps; each step's discussion; step 1 is the description.\n","title":"cycle: each step is the main screen, driven by a [cycle] protocol"}},{"kind":"set-status","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792679410,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5978897776"},"data":{"status":"closed"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792679413,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5978897776"},"data":{"add":["kind:feat","prio:p1","risk:structural","status:done","assignee:guilbep"],"remove":null}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792679409,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6343271035"},"data":{"body":"M1 (the protocol) and M2 (one page) landed in #39 (merge 9ebd259). M3 to M6 go on under b768fbb. ADR 0001, section 9, amends the PRD's step 4: a run that counts happens in a clean checkout."}}]}